        "note": "The Caffarelli-Kohn-Nirenberg formalization (Armstrong, Vicol) is a Lake dependency pinned to the exact commit 381d658ead0f03a18361965cc0427ce3fa5844ab (both libraries use Lean's module system). Its suitable-weak-solution class, regular and singular points, and Theorems A and C are used unchanged. Since 2026-09-29 it also contains the Leray background moved out of this repository: the definitions CKN.IsInJ, CKN.IsLerayHopfSolution, CKN.IsGlobalLerayHopfSolution, CKN.IsForcedLerayHopfSolution, CKN.IsGlobalForcedLerayHopfSolution, CKN.IsLocallySquareIntegrableForce, CKN.IsLocallyQIntegrableForce, CKN.forcedQuadraticTensor and CKN.HasSpaceTimeWeakDerivs, and the theorems CKN.leray_existence, CKN.leray_existence_singularSet, CKN.associatedPressure, CKN.lerayExistenceForced, CKN.lerayExistenceForcedSingularSet and CKN.associatedPressureForced. These six theorems are results of that dependency and are not main results of this repository. CKN's Leray comparator pair restates five of them; CKN.associatedPressureForced has no comparator restatement.",
